[15.010583, "o", "Help on class TestingSource in module bytewax.testing:\r\n\r\nclass T\bTe\bes\bst\bti\bin\bng\bgS\bSo\bou\bur\brc\bce\be(bytewax.inputs.FixedPartitionedSource)\r\n |  TestingSource(ib: Iterable[Union[~X, bytewax.testing.TestingSource.EOF, bytewax.testing.TestingSource.ABORT, bytewax.testing.TestingSource.PAUSE]], batch_si\r\nze: int = 1)\r\n |\r\n |  Produce input from a Python iterable.\r\n |\r\n |  You only want to use this for unit testing.\r\n |\r\n |  The iterable must be identical on all workers.\r\n |\r\n |  There is no parallelism; only one worker will actually consume the\r\n |  iterable.\r\n |\r\n"]
[15.01069, "o", " |  Be careful using a generator as the iterable; if you fail and\r\n |  attempt to resume the dataflow without rebuilding it, the\r\n |  half-consumed generator will be re-used on recovery and early\r\n |  input will be lost so resume will see the correct data.\r\n |\r\n |  Method resolution order:\r\n |      TestingSource\r\n |      bytewax.inputs.FixedPartitionedSource\r\n |      bytewax.inputs.Source\r\n |      abc.ABC\r\n |      typing.Generic\r\n |      builtins.object\r\n |\r\n |  Methods defined here:\r\n |\r\n |  _\b__\b_i\bin\bni\bit\bt_\b__\b_(self, ib: Iterable[Union[~X, bytewax.testing.TestingSource.EOF, bytewax.testing.TestingSource.ABORT, bytewax.testing.TestingSource.PAUSE]], batch_s\r\nize: int = 1)\r\n |      Init.\r\n |\r\n |      :arg ib: Iterable for input.\r\n |\r\n |      :arg batch_size: Number of items from the iterable to emit in\r\n |          each batch. Defaults to 1.\r\n |\r\n\u001b[7m--More--\u001b[27m"]
